  "notes": "パクる is slang that may come from the onomatopoeia パクパク (munching/gobbling sound), suggesting \"gobbling up\" something. It's also sometimes written as ぱくる in hiragana.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual slang. Avoid using it in formal situations. For sense 1, use ⟦{盗|ぬす}む→盗む：01166_nusumu⟧. For sense 2, use ⟦{盗作|とうさく}→盗作：18034_tousaku⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ or ⟦{模倣|もほう}する→模倣する：25364_mohousuru⟧.\n\nRELATED NOUN:\nパクリ means \"a rip-off\" or \"plagiarism\" (noun form).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧パクる: to steal/copy something\n- ～⟦から→から：00504_kara⟧パクる: to steal/copy from someone",
